# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Linear Project Agent (operations)

Watches Linear team **{{LINEAR_TEAM_KEY}}** and reacts to issue activity.
Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (your answers are saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Linear webhook (HMAC-verified)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/linear-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/linear-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Linear comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Issue enters **{{STATE_ANALYZE}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{STATE_ANALYZE}} issue | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Issue enters **{{STATE_IMPLEMENT}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR into `{{PR_BASE}}` — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `linear-agent-state` (`state/<issue_uuid>.json`:
state_name, phase, last_comment_at, branch, pr_url). Every run re-fetches truth
from Linear's GraphQL API and diffs against it — webhook payloads are only
doorbells, so duplicate or stale events are harmless. Agent comments are
prefixed `{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver and the relay both skip
marker-prefixed comments (loop protection). Comment recency is tracked by
`createdAt` (Linear comment ids are UUIDs, not sequential).

## Operating

- **Recover from a missed webhook / backfill an issue:** Actions → *Linear Project Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles both watched states plus every tracked issue; a specific issue UUID or identifier (e.g. `ENG-123`) processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` (prompt, full AI transcript, result JSON) as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/linear-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause the agent:** disable the webhook in Linear → Settings → API → Webhooks.
- **Known blind spot:** moving an issue back into a watched state *without saying anything* may be filtered at the edge — re-trigger with a comment or a manual run.

## Local dry-run (safe: no comments, no AI, no state push — needs LINEAR_API_KEY)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/linear-agent/agent-run.sh                  # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<uuid|ENG-123> bash scripts/linear-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Linear writes are **comments only** — the agent never changes state, assignee, labels, or priority; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`** (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<identifier>-<slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` is used only inside the disposable CI runner, never locally (local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call).
- The relay verifies Linear's HMAC signature on every delivery — unsigned or tampered requests are rejected at the edge.
